# ─── DaySync Environment Variables ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Supabase Project Configuration (From Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API)
# Supports both Vite standard (VITE_) and Vercel / Next.js (NEXT_PUBLIC_) prefixes:
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-public-key

# Optional alias for Vercel / Next.js environments
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-public-key

# ─── Supabase Auth Google Provider Setup Instructions ──────────────────────
# 1. In Google Cloud Console:
#    - Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web Application)
#    - Set Authorized redirect URI to: https://your-project-id.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# 2. In Supabase Dashboard:
#    - Navigate to Authentication -> Providers -> Google
#    - Enable Google provider
#    - Paste Google Client ID and Google Client Secret
#    - Set Redirect URL to your deployed DaySync URL (e.g., https://your-daysync.vercel.app or http://localhost:5173)
